EXT. DRAINED BACKYARD POOL - DAY

Cracked blue paint. Leaves in the deep end. Two boards leaned against the lip. Heat bends the air.

MOSES AGYEMAN, 15, hoodie, scabbed knees, stands at the top of the transition. JAI KAPOOR, 15, a cap on backward, a stolen helmet, grips the coping with both hands.

He drops in. He wobbles. He rolls out.

He grins. He doesn't see the other one.

He drops in too, harder, faster, and clips the edge of the first board. Both skate out and slam into the shallow end together, a tangle of wheels and limbs.

He laughs first. Then he does. Then neither can breathe.

He pulls himself up. He pulls him up. Blood on a palm. Dust on a cheek.

MOSES
You see that?

JAI
I felt that.

MOSES
That was clean.

JAI
That was a car crash.

MOSES
Again?

JAI
Again.

They climb the ladder. Side by side. Neither says it. Both are too happy to say it.
